*** Test Cases ***

[1]CB008940-Q_B2_IWK_CB8862_DL_Adaptive_Retransmission
    [Documentation] 
    ...     Conditions:      
    ...     Conditions:     NrCell1 : DL and UL data transmission is continuously ongoing for the UE1
    ...                     NrCell2 : DL and UL data transmission is continuously ongoing for the UE2
    ...                     NrCell3 : DL and UL data transmission is continuously ongoing for the UE2
    ...     Actions:        The radio conditions change continuously from good to worse
	...                     and vice versa to trigger HARQ retransmissions
	...                     If the adaptive retransmission scheme is not applied the retransmission is granted with the initial MCS 
    ...                     or rather postponed if the retransmission cannot be scheduled
	...                     If the adaptive retransmission scheme is applied for HARQ retransmissions in DL and UL
	...                     a reserved MCS is used for the adaptive retransmission condition
	...     Checks:         With activation of the PRB pooling feature the number of UEs with initial transmission 
    ...                     and HARQ retransmission scheduled during the slot is decreased 
    ...                     because the number of available PRBs in the cell is restricted
	...                     The algorithm of the adaptive retransmission may reduce for one UE with an HARQ retransmission 
    ...                     the number of PRBs to the configured minimum allocation size
     ...    Verdict:        For each HARQ process index , redundancy version index derives from number of HARQ transmission 
     ...                    according to the following RvSequence : RV0, RV2, RV3 and RV1

    TC 8940 Interaction with CB008662 DL Retransmission
    ...                                                             ${IWK_CB008662}
    ...                                                             ${Vendor_IWK_CB8940-Q_CB7113} 
    ...                                                             ${dict_settings_3_UEs_Dl_Ul_Low_Tput} 
    ...                                                             nrCell=3
  #  [Teardown]    Run Keyword If Test Failed    Setup.Test Teardown
    [Teardown]    Display diagnosis 

[1]CB008940-Q_B2_IWK_CB8862_UL_Adaptive_Retransmission
    [Documentation]    
    ...     Conditions:     NrCell1 : DL and UL data transmission is continuously ongoing for the UE1
    ...                     NrCell2 : DL and UL data transmission is continuously ongoing for the UE2
    ...                     NrCell3 : DL and UL data transmission is continuously ongoing for the UE2
    ...     Actions:        The link conditions change continuously from good to worse
	...                     and vice versa to trigger HARQ retransmissions
	...                     Without CB8662 adaptive retransmission scheme applied the retransmission is granted with the initial MCS 
    ...                     or rather postponed if the retransmission cannot be scheduled
	...                     With CB8662 adaptive retransmission scheme applied for HARQ retransmissions in DL and UL
	...                     a reserved MCS is used for the adaptive retransmission condition
	...     Checks:         With activation of the PRB pooling feature the number of UEs with initial transmission 
    ...                     and HARQ retransmission scheduled during the slot is decreased 
    ...                     because the number of available PRBs in the cell is restricted
	...                     The algorithm of the adaptive retransmission may reduce for one UE with an HARQ retransmission 
    ...                     the number of PRBs to the configured minimum allocation size
     ...    Verdict:        For each HARQ process index , redundancy version index derives from number of HARQ transmission 
     ...                    according to the following RvSequence : RV0, RV2, RV3 and RV1
